<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
  Purely informational - HediffSet_GetHungerRateFactor_Patch.cs is what actually makes
  the Nuclear Battery reduce a sapient mech's hunger rate; nothing here changes behavior.
  Without this, the only way to know the hediff does that on a sapient mech is prior
  knowledge of this mod's own source or checking the inspect tab's hunger-rate math by
  hand - appending a line to the hediff's own description makes it discoverable in the
  normal tooltip instead. Gated on Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core being installed - without it,
  DMS_NuclearBattery doesn't exist for the xpath to match.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace" MayRequire="Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core">
    <xpath>Defs/HediffDef[defName="DMS_NuclearBattery"]/description</xpath>
    <value>
      <description>The abundant output of installed nuclear-powered quantum batteries eliminates the need to recharge. The reactor can be overloaded to produce a chain reaction meltdown comparable to an anti-grain warhead.\n\nOn a sapient mechanoid, which no longer runs on mech energy, this instead reduces its hunger rate by that same factor.</description>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
